      },
      "message": "fix(ui): the near plane and the ortho eye stay with the zoom\n\nTwo ways the viewport ate the model from its own camera:\n\n- Perspective: the near plane was a fixed 0.1 mm from the eye, so at\n  close zoom (the minimum dolly is 0.5 mm) the geometry in front of\n  the near plane clipped instead of rendering - the view went through\n  the model. The near plane now rides dist (0.1 % of the view depth,\n  clamped to 1e-5 min, 0.1 max).\n- Orthographic: the eye travelled with dist, so zooming dollied the\n  eye into the model and clipped through its faces from inside. The\n  eye now sits at a fixed nominal distance (100 mm) behind the target\n  and dist is only a scale factor, the way the view box's half-height\n  was always meant to work.",
